{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the king of Egypt died.</b> As long as that king was alive, they were hoping for when he would die — perhaps the decree would be annulled. And when he died and it was not annulled, they said: from now we know that there is no end to this — therefore ויאנחו. Another explanation: וימת מלך מצרים ויאנחו — since the king died, Moses could return to Egypt, and also the children of Israel sighed, and also the Holy One, blessed be He, remembered His covenant. All these things caused that Moses was sent."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:29.875305470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}